1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,460
“I think someone has done sorcery on me”... a sentence we hear often,

2
00:00:04,550 --> 00:00:07,530
from a wife whose bond with her husband suddenly went cold,

3
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:11,240
from a young woman whose suitors come and then leave, one after another,

4
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:15,580
and from a young man whose work, studies and whole life seem to be tied up in knots.

5
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:18,970
But the real question is: how do we actually know?

6
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,040
Is every knot in life sorcery?

7
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:25,480
And why do some people go for the answer to the very people who write sorcery?

8
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:30,580
Today we answer this from the Qur’an, the Sunnah and the books of scholars of ruqyah.

9
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:33,560
First of all: no one knows the unseen except Allah.

10
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:40,050
No human can tell you with certainty: “You are bewitched, so-and-so did it, and the sorcery is buried in such a place.”

11
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:44,620
Allah says: “Say: none in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen except Allah.”

12
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:49,830
Whoever claims it is either making it up or receiving it from jinn and soothsayers.

13
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:57,460
And he (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever goes to a soothsayer or fortune-teller and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad.”

14
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:02,570
So what practitioners mention are signs to take as hints, not certainty to build upon.

15
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:10,190
Signs by type of sorcery: scholars of ruqyah divide sorcery by its aim and mention signs for each type.

16
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,660
Type one: the sorcery of separation,

17
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:16,790
about which Allah said: “what separates a man from his wife.”

18
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:21,230
Among its signs: love suddenly turning into hatred,

19
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:26,390
with no notable incident, and small things blowing up until quarrels are about nothing,

20
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:30,900
frequent suspicions, and one spouse seeing the other as ugly,

21
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:36,350
or being repelled by the place where the other sits, while outside the house things are as usual.

22
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:39,400
Type two: the sorcery that blocks marriage:

23
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:45,650
a suitor comes and is happy, then suddenly backs out for no reason, and this repeats again and again,

24
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:51,150
or the young woman or man feels tightness whenever marriage is mentioned, and refuses without reason.

25
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:54,150
Type three: the sorcery of lethargy:

26
00:01:54,240 --> 00:02:04,080
love of isolation and silence, much sleep, constant listlessness, a scattered mind, and abandoning work or study one used to love.

27
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:10,120
Type four: the sorcery of attraction; it does not aim to separate but to win over a certain heart,

28
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:17,820
its signs: sudden excessive love that reason can’t accept, intense anxiety when apart, and blind obedience.

29
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:20,890
Type five: the sorcery of illusion.

30
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:26,130
Allah says of Pharaoh’s sorcerers: “It seemed to him from their magic that they were moving.”

31
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:31,970
The bewitched sees things other than they are: the still as moving, the small as large.

32
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:38,080
And general signs: practitioners mention signs common to most types:

33
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:45,230
recurring nightmares, especially of frightening animals, falling from a height, or someone chasing the sleeper,

34
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:52,420
tightness and heaviness in the chest at the adhan or on hearing the Qur’an, and a sudden strong aversion to prayer and dhikr,

35
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:58,540
and finding strange things in the house or among belongings: knots, hair and written papers.

36
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:04,570
But they are not conclusive; each of these signs can have another cause.

37
00:03:04,660 --> 00:03:08,420
Marital conflict may come from a sharp tongue and too many demands,

38
00:03:08,510 --> 00:03:14,030
difficulties may be a test from Allah, and heaviness in worship may come from sins and heedlessness.

39
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:21,190
Allah says: “Whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much.”

40
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:24,970
The worst thing we can do is accuse a relative or neighbour on suspicion.

41
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:33,130
The Prophet (peace be upon him) was bewitched and knew who did it, yet he said: “I disliked stirring up evil among people because of it.”

42
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:36,650
How do you recognise a sorcerer? Many people don’t know this:

43
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,790
sometimes the person we go to for undoing sorcery is the sorcerer himself.

44
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:46,420
Scholars of ruqyah mention signs that expose him: he asks for your name and your mother’s name,

45
00:03:46,510 --> 00:03:49,560
asks for something of your clothes, hair or nails,

46
00:03:49,650 --> 00:03:57,950
asks for an animal of a certain colour or description to slaughter, perhaps without mentioning Allah’s name, perhaps telling you to smear something with its blood,

47
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,590
mutters unintelligible words,

48
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:06,160
gives you a paper with tables, numbers and broken-up letters and tells you to hang it up,

49
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:11,330
tells you to isolate yourself for days in a dark room, or not to touch water for a while,

50
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:16,140
gives you something to bury, or a paper to burn and inhale its smoke,

51
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:21,350
and he may tell you your name, your town and your problem before you speak, to dazzle you.

52
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:26,190
If you see any of this, know you are in the wrong place; get up and leave.

53
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:34,130
He (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever hangs an amulet has committed shirk,” and of undoing sorcery with sorcery: “It is the work of the devil.”

54
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,940
So what is the right way?

55
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:39,260
If certainty is not possible, the answer is simple:

56
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:43,600
sharʿī ruqyah, which is both a test and a treatment at the same time:

57
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:50,100
if there is sorcery, Allah nullifies it by His leave; if not, it is remembrance, healing and blessing, with no harm in it.

58
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:59,860
Practitioners mention that the bewitched may feel heaviness, repeated yawning or tears during ruqyah, then lightness and relief after some sessions.

59
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,680
And here is the plan:

60
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:08,140
First: the verses that nullify sorcery, recited over yourself or over water. From Sūrat al-Aʿrāf:

61
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:16,500
“And We inspired Moses: throw your staff, and at once it swallowed what they had faked. So the truth prevailed, and what they were doing was nullified.”

62
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:23,920
From Sūrat Yūnus: “What you have brought is sorcery; Allah will surely nullify it. Allah does not set right the work of corrupters.”

63
00:05:24,010 --> 00:05:25,520
From Sūrat Ṭā Hā:

64
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:30,600
“What they have made is only a sorcerer’s trick, and the sorcerer will not succeed wherever he comes.”

65
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:34,900
Along with them: al-Fātiḥa, Āyat al-Kursī, the end of al-Baqara, and al-Ikhlāṣ, al-Falaq and an-Nās.

66
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:37,610
Second: water and lote-tree leaves.

67
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:45,130
It is reported from some of the early generations, and Ibn Ḥajar cites it in Fatḥ al-Bārī: seven green lote leaves are crushed and placed in water,

68
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:52,690
Āyat al-Kursī, the Muʿawwidhāt and the sorcery verses are recited over it, then three sips are drunk and the rest used for washing.

69
00:05:52,770 --> 00:05:56,710
Third: Sūrat al-Baqara.

70
00:05:56,800 --> 00:06:06,450
“Recite Sūrat al-Baqara, for taking it is a blessing, leaving it is a regret, and al-baṭala cannot withstand it,” al-baṭala being the sorcerers, who cannot bear Sūrat al-Baqara.

71
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:08,590
Fourth: ʿajwa dates.

72
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:16,080
He (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever eats seven ʿajwa dates every morning, no poison or sorcery will harm him that day.”

73
00:06:16,170 --> 00:06:20,430
Fifth: the morning and evening adhkār, and keeping up the prayer,

74
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:25,180
and with them this dhikr a hundred times a day, a protection from the devil until evening:

75
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:31,560
“There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; His is the dominion and His the praise, and He is capable of all things.”

76
00:06:31,650 --> 00:06:37,020
Sixth: patience, for treating sorcery may take weeks and months,

77
00:06:37,110 --> 00:06:40,760
so don’t despair, and don’t turn back from the lawful way to the way of sorcerers.

78
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:43,930
So if you ask: how do I know I am bewitched?

79
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:47,510
The answer: know the signs, but don’t judge by them,

80
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:52,130
don’t go to anyone who claims knowledge of the unseen, and don’t accuse anyone,

81
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:58,330
and begin with sharʿī ruqyah; if there is sorcery, Allah has promised: “Allah will surely nullify it.”

82
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:02,940
Send this clip to someone living in this fear, and write in the comments:

83
00:07:03,030 --> 00:07:06,310
“O Allah, undo every knot and every sorcery from our lives.”

84
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:07,140
Amen.

